"The goggles' overlay will be in your stream" = "The goggles' overlay will be in your stream";
"The goggles draw their own on-screen display (flight data, battery, storage warnings) into the picture they send, so it appears in OBS, recordings and streams too.\n\nYou can turn it off on the goggles, or crop it out here with Output framing. That crop only affects what you record and stream; the preview stays as it is.\n\nTip: to crop the picture later but keep the overlay's data in the original, set the goggles' display scale to about 70%. The picture then sits inside the frame and a centred crop of about 1.4x (Output framing zoom, or your editor) removes the overlay." = "The goggles draw their own on-screen display (flight data, battery, storage warnings) into the picture they send, so it appears in OBS, recordings and streams too.\n\nYou can turn it off on the goggles, or crop it out here with Output framing. That crop only affects what you record and stream; the preview stays as it is.\n\nTip: to crop the picture later but keep the overlay's data in the original, set the goggles' display scale to about 70%. The picture then sits inside the frame and a centred crop of about 1.4x (Output framing zoom, or your editor) removes the overlay.";
